<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23070" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-explēbĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		2. in-expleo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that cannot be filled</i>, <i>insatiable</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inexplebilis potu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 25, 30, § 88</span></i>
			. stomachus, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 89 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populi fauces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rep. 1, 43, 66</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cupiditas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 5, 6, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vir inexplebilis virtutis veraeque laudis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					28, 17, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">honorum fames,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					3, 21, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colloquiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. ad Helv. 15, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
